VALIDATION / INTERPRETATION
- Standard travel/riding time keeps weight 1.0.
- Access/egress time is weighted 1.5.
- Waiting time is weighted 2.0.
- These multipliers are explicit behavioural assumptions, not measured preferences.
- Pareto efficiency is independent of VOT.
- A Pareto-efficient mode cannot be made both cheaper and faster by another observed mode.
- PT marginal-cost sensitivity distinguishes accounting allocation from the cost of an additional trip with an already-owned pass.
